I Completed the **Network Discovery Detection** room on TryHackMe

This hands-on lab focused on understanding how attackers perform network reconnaissance and how defenders can identify and investigate 
discovery activity using network telemetry and log analysis.

## Topics Covered

* Network discovery fundamentals
* External vs internal scanning and their security impact
* Host discovery and ping sweeps
* Port scanning techniques
* Horizontal vs vertical scanning
* TCP SYN scans and scan-state analysis
* Understanding network reconnaissance behavior
* Detection of malicious scanning activity
* Traffic analysis using Zeek connection logs
* Interpreting `zeek.conn.conn_state` values

## Tools & Technologies Used

* Kibana
* Elasticsearch
* Zeek
* Linux command-line utilities
* AWK for log parsing and filtering

## Techniques Practiced

* Log analysis and threat hunting
* Identifying external reconnaissance activity
* Detecting internal scanning behavior
* Analyzing TCP connection states AND UDP Scan
* Investigating subnet-wide ping sweeps
* Correlating source and destination IP activity
* Identifying scan patterns across multiple ports and hosts

This room strengthened my practical understanding of network reconnaissance detection and improved my ability to analyze real-world 
scanning activity using SIEM and network security monitoring tools.

